<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21187] Closing a File After FLR Mirror Merge/Split Incorrectly Bypasses Permission Checks</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21187</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When a client closes a file normally, the MDS temporarily grants extra permissions to avoid unnecessary permission checks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, these extra permissions should not be granted when closing a file also involves changes to its layout. This is already handled correctly for HSM release and layout swap operations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same restriction was missing for FLR mirror merge and split operations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As a result, closing a file after merging or splitting FLR mirrors could receive extra permissions and bypass normal security checks, including the immutable file check.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Expected Behavior: The MDS should not grant extra permissions when closing a file after an FLR mirror merge or split, just as it does for HSM release and layout swap operations.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
